    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0610" n="504" xml:id="pg504"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure A.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Black to Col.
                            Lindhamer</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Nuremberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-01-26"><hi rendition="#italic">January 26,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: His excellency the minister of the
                    United States of America at Berlin instructs me to inquire whether John or
                    Johann Haberacker or Haberacher is still serving in the fourteenth infantry
                    regiment therefore have the honor to requst that you will kindly give me the
                    desired information at your earliest convenience and the date of his discharge
                    in case it has takeji place. I am instructed to give his excellency information
                    by telegraph.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. J. Black</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
